.TH NESTWG 1 "August 2026" "nestwg" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nestwg \- create and manage nested WireGuard VPN chains
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nestwg validate
.IR chain.yaml
.br
.B nestwg plan
.IR chain.yaml
.br
.B nestwg up
.RB [ --wait " duration]
.IR chain.yaml
.br
.B nestwg down
.IR chain-name
.br
.B nestwg status
.RI [ chain-name ]
.br
.B nestwg exec
.I chain-name
.B --
.I command
.RI [ arguments... ]
.br
.B nestwg shell
.IR chain-name
.br
.B nestwg doctor
.br
.B nestwg recover
.I chain-name
.br
.B nestwg version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nestwg
constructs ordered WireGuard tunnels inside Linux network namespaces. Each
inner WireGuard socket is born in the plaintext network exposed by the
previous hop, forcing its encrypted transport through that hop. The payload
network contains only loopback and the innermost WireGuard interface.
.PP
The chain document orders hops from the outermost entry to the innermost exit.
Endpoint hostnames are resolved and pinned before privileged network changes.
Plans and runtime state do not contain private or preshared keys.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B validate
Strictly parse the chain and referenced WireGuard files without changing the
host.
.TP
.B plan
Print the executable JSON plan, including pinned endpoints, namespace names,
interface addresses, allowed routes, and calculated MTUs.
.TP
.B up
Create a persistent chain. With
.BR --wait ,
wait until every hop has completed a WireGuard handshake or the duration
expires. A readiness timeout leaves the configured chain up for inspection.
.TP
.B down
Remove a chain in reverse order. Teardown refuses to proceed while a
NestWG-managed payload command holds a shared lifecycle lock.
.TP
.B status
Show active chains and live handshake and transfer information.
.TP
.B exec
Run one command in the fail-closed payload network with private DNS mounts.
When invoked via sudo, the command runs as the invoking user.
.TP
.B shell
Open the invoking user's shell in the payload network.
.TP
.B doctor
Check privileges, netlink access, kernel WireGuard support, resolver mounting,
and runtime-state security.
.TP
.B recover
Remove strictly named, process-free orphan namespaces after a chain state file
has been lost. Recovery refuses active namespaces and chains that still have a
state record.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/nestwg
Root-owned mode-0700 locks, recovery state, and per-chain resolver files.
.TP
.I /run/netns/nwg-<chain>-*
Named network namespaces owned by a chain.
.SH SECURITY
WireGuard configuration files must not be accessible by group or other users.
Hook commands from wg-quick files are ignored and never executed. Application
protocol encryption such as TLS remains necessary; the exit can observe
plaintext application traffic and final destinations.
.PP
NestWG is pre-release software and must not yet be relied upon as a security or
anonymity boundary. See SECURITY.md and docs/threat-model.md.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Lifecycle and inspection commands return zero on success and nonzero on
validation, readiness, privilege, or kernel-operation failure. The
.B exec
and
.B shell
commands preserve the payload process exit status.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wg (8),
.BR ip-netns (8),
.BR wireguard (8)
